{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesViaMarkovTrace","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones_pos","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L211-L220","doc":"**`nuclearQuotientJones` is positive** in the Wenzl regime — every branch of\nthe selection is a positive torus-link value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesTrefoil_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesTrefoil_pos","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L203-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesHopfLink_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesHopfLink_pos","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L196-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesUnknot_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesUnknot_pos","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L193-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.heckeH_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.heckeH_pos","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L187-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.markovZ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.markovZ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L183-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones_oddZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones_oddZ","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L169-L176","doc":"An **odd-`Z`, non-double-magic** nucleus maps to the trefoil value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones_evenZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones_evenZ","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L160-L167","doc":"An **even-`Z`, non-double-magic** nucleus maps to the Hopf-link value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones_doubleMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones_doubleMagic","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L152-L158","doc":"A **double-magic** nucleus maps to the unknot value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearQuotientJones","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L141-L150","doc":"**The nuclear quotient braid Jones value** — the RHS of the (open) Part-4\nconjecture `a(Z,N) = J_β̄(q)`. Selects the `(2,k)` torus-link Jones value by\nthe shell-structure crossing power `k = nuclearCrossingPower Z N`. This is the\nconcrete construction of `jet_filtered_knot_factor.jonesQuotient`; it does\n**not** assert equality with the BW knot factor `a(Z,N)` (the open\nconjecture). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearCrossingPower_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearCrossingPower_mem","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L130-L139","doc":"The crossing power is always one of the three torus-link indices `{1,2,3}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearCrossingPower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.nuclearCrossingPower","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L123-L128","doc":"**Crossing power `k` of the nuclear quotient braid** `β̄`, per\n`jet-filtered-knot-factor.md`: `1` (unknot) if double-magic, else `2` (Hopf)\nif `Z` even, else `3` (trefoil, `Z` odd). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.isMagicNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.isMagicNumber","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L120-L121","doc":"Whether `n` is a magic number (closed shell). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.magicNumbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.magicNumbers","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L117-L118","doc":"The nuclear magic numbers (closed-shell nucleon counts). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesHopfLink_eq_jonesHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesHopfLink_eq_jonesHopf","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L91-L115","doc":"**The Hopf-value bridge**: the `(h·z + 1)` Hopf value here equals the\ncanonical closed form `jonesHopf` of [`JonesViaMarkovTrace`].\n\n**Under convention D this stopped needing an `rpow` normalisation at all**\n(2026-08-26, bean `qou-cxjq`). It used to be \"the `rpow`-normalisation\nbridge, previously deferred pending the LSP\": both sides reduced to\n`√q − 1/√q + 1`, and the proof had to convert `Real.sqrt q ↔ q ^ (1/2 : ℝ)`,\nestablish `q ^ (5/2) = q² · √q`, and clear denominators around a square root.\n\nUnder D both sides are the *same rational function* `(q⁴ + 1)/(q² + 1)` — the\nMarkov axiom fixes `tr_M(σ₁²) = h·z + 1`, and at `z = q³/(q²+1)` that is\nexactly the tower's migrated `trM_sigma1_sq`. The square roots are gone from\nboth, so the bridge is `field_simp; ring`.\n\nWorth noting against the general expectation that a convention migration costs\nproof effort: here it *removed* a proof obligation that had been deferred. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesTrefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesTrefoil","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L87-L89","doc":"**Jones value of the trefoil** `= (2,3)` torus link\n`= tr_M(σ₁³) = (h²+1)·z + h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesHopfLink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesHopfLink","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L83-L85","doc":"**Jones value of the Hopf link** `= (2,2)` torus link `= tr_M(σ₁²) = h·z + 1`.\nCoincides with `JonesViaMarkovTrace.jonesHopf` (sympy Δ = 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesUnknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.jonesUnknot","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L80-L81","doc":"**Jones value of the unknot** `= (2,1)` torus link `= tr_M(σ₁) = z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.markovZ","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L68-L78","doc":"The canonical Markov parameter in **convention D**, `z = q³/(q² + 1)` — the\nsame value carried by `markovTraceTower_canonical`.\n\n**Migrated from convention C 2026-08-26 (bean `qou-cxjq`).** This read\n`1/(√q + 1/√q)` = `√q/(q+1)`, convention C. The \"same value carried by\n`markovTraceTower_canonical`\" clause is why this file had to move in the same\ntranche as that instance: the tower migrated to D first, which made this\ndocstring's claim FALSE for exactly as long as the two disagreed. A\ncross-reference between two same-named quantities is only as good as the\nconvention they share. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.heckeH","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesNuclearQuotient.lean#L65-L66","doc":"The Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹` (AGENTS.md §7a: `σ² = h·σ + 1`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}